# SD: Compact documented approvals with truthful version links

Status: draft
Gate: SD
Gate approval: open
Owner: Arndt Gold
Date: 2026-10-09
Run: cockpit-documented-approvals-20261009-01
Language: en
Traceability contract: criteria-chain-v1
Design Decisions contract: sd-decisions-v1

## Solution Overview

Implement the approved comparable approval overview only within the existing selected undertaking presentation. The same ordered approval rows serve broad three-column and narrow stacked arrangements, without replacing current control assessment, surrounding evidence sections or draft-check UI. Each recorded approved gate contributes one row: document name, deliberate documented-evidence disclosure and a truthfully labelled current-resource action or unavailable state. The count is derived from those exact Core facts, not a fixed four-document list.

A small internal DocumentedApprovals presentation component will separate this bounded block from WorkStep's current-work assessment. It consumes the existing typed approved rows, same-Run registered resources, onOpen and sourceDisabled; it introduces no public DTO, persistence, permission or validation service. WorkStep remains the integration owner. Semantic list items contain three labelled groups, arranged by a scoped CSS grid. A shared visible column heading in wide mode assists comparison; row-level labels and contextual accessible action names preserve meaning in narrow mode. Native details/summary keep original evidence deliberately folded. The same DOM and stable keys remain across widths, avoiding remount-driven focus/disclosure/scroll loss.

The only supported document-version classification is current registered source or unavailable. Existing evidence has no certified readable historical-version binding. Do not introduce an approved-version selector, speculative certification branch, fake verified fixture or parser of partial hashes/prose. “Freigegebene Fassung ansehen” cannot be emitted from today's DTO. A future canonical certification capability would require its own separately governed contract change.

This is a proposed design, not implemented behavior or test/host success. PRD acceptance is the sole product authority; this SD describes its realization without redefining it.

