## Risks And Open Questions

No material product/design question remains open with the inspected inputs. Accepted historical-proof absence is a transparent product limitation, not an archive obligation. Responsive density and document focus may regress if old general list spacing leaks into the new block; scoped styles and actual rendered cases address that risk. Earlier changes are dirty and require baseline containment before code. Any observed new authority or public-contract requirement is a routing blocker rather than an inferred extension. Native proof limitations must stay explicit if the currently available host cannot load the future build; no new host activation is assumed by this design.

